I've implemented GMS-106 on GMS-106-safe-player-start and it compiles, but nothing has been run in the Editor yet. The final step, checking it in PIE, needs you.

What changed
- Spawn location: the player now starts on a cell chosen from the map data instead of wherever the PlayerStart was placed. A cell qualifies as a safe start when it and all eight cells around it are playable, which keeps the character at least a full tile away from the boundary walls.
- Which cell: of those, it picks the one closest to the centre of the playable area, so each map always starts in the same place.
- Props: before using a cell, it checks that the character's capsule doesn't overlap any blocking prop placed in the level. If it does, it tries the next cell.
- Map selection: it reads LevelToRender from the level's ATileMapRenderer, so PlayGame1 and PlayGame2 both work, and a newly registered map works with no extra code.
- Facing: the PlayerStart's yaw is still used, so the starting camera direction is set in the Editor as before.
- Failure: if nothing works, it logs an error and falls back to the PlayerStart. If there isn't even a start spot, it logs an error and spawns nothing, with no crash.

